      {
        "text": "Mike Fong has represented the 49th State Assembly District since 2022. He previously served as a trustee for the Los Angeles Community College District, a deputy mayor, and a city councilmember's aide. His passed 2025-2026 bills included AB 2436 on tuition for Team USA athletes and AB 2392 on generative artificial intelligence training at public colleges. In 2023, he said he planned to push for stronger gun safety laws and violence prevention funding. In 2023, he proposed a bill shortening the deadline for prohibited persons to turn over firearms from five days to two. His campaign says he is addressing climate change and homelessness. His website states he has secured $35 million for local parks and community centers.",
